  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 100 AM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nStrong high pressure keeps us baking thru the weekend. Highs\nyesterday were largely in the mid-upper 90s, with some lower \n90s northeast, and HI's topped out in the 102-113 degree range,\nwith most sites settling in the 105-110 degree range. We should\nsee similar output this weekend, with maximum air temperatures \nAOA yesterday's numbers, reaching around 100 degrees even (SEMO \nOzarks) as dew points hover in their same ballpark. The \nprolonged duration Extreme Heat Warning thus continues for all \nlocalities thru the weekend.\n\nAny near term weekend pops will be glancing blow pops, from the\nupstream action to our north that tops the ridge and spills \ndown toward I-70. Further south down here, a 12-13C cap at H7 \nwill be tough to overcome with little/no forcing offered til the\nactual front drops into the picture. Its Sunday night passage \nis when pops pick up with a little bit more earnest and the \nstifling air mass is turned over as northerlies draw in some \n(relative to the extreme heat) cooler/drier air to begin the new\nwork week, ceasing our headlines with a return to more \nclimatologically 'normal' temperatures and humidity.\n\nAnother front's mid week passage leads to an additional pops\nspike by Wednesday night. This one results in a nice, \nreinforcing shot of cooler and drier air that might well bring \nsome pleasantry in the form of highs in the 80s again as dew \npoints drop into, and possibly? thru the 60s, if all pans out as\nit looks now.",
